NUM-30: route pervious runoff onto IMPERV0 when there is no IMPERV1 area

With RouteTo IMPERVIOUS only (1 - PctRouted) of the pervious runoff goes to
the outlet; the rest is meant to arrive next step as inflow to the
impervious area with depression storage (IMPERV1). RunoffSolver::execute()
skipped that transfer when IMPERV1 has no area (PctZero = 100), so the
routed share left the pervious sub-area and was never added anywhere. Send
it to IMPERV0, the only impervious sub-area in that case (the same change
as the 5.3.0 patch).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-30_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
index aa81dc7..bd6a301 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
@@ -587,6 +587,11 @@ void RunoffSolver::execute(SimulationContext& ctx, double dt, double evap_rate_i
             double q = soa_.old_runoff_perv[ui];
             runon_imperv1 += q * (1.0 - f_outlet) * fp / f1;
         }
+        else if (route_mode == 1 && f0 > 0.0) {
+            // PctZero = 100: no IMPERV1 area, so onto IMPERV0
+            double q = soa_.old_runoff_perv[ui];
+            runon_imperv0 += q * (1.0 - f_outlet) * fp / f0;
+        }
 
         // Gap #23: LID return flow to pervious area (legacy lid_getFlowToPerv
         // in subcatch_getRunon — one-step lag), after the transfer above.
